## 4. Remaining p=5 bottleneck

The immediate finite target is now bounded:

- profile (3 singleton, 1 pair): m=3,4,5,6 only, with only two m=6 support
  orbits;
- profile (5 singleton): m=3,4,5,6,7 only, with only ten m=7 support orbits and
  two possible m=7 multiplicity profiles.

The next highest-value exact certificate is the m=7 five-singleton layer. It
should enumerate the ten support orbits, the two multiplicity profiles,
five singleton placements satisfying touched-complete nullity at most one,
all cycle orientations, singleton local directions spanning rank-three P with
generalized weights at least (2,4,5), the quotient-basis cover/transversal
filters, and finally require external relation-rank increment exactly six.

This note does not close the p=5 branch, the nine-no-root k=6 layer, C-II, or
Level I.
